Well, it depends what you do with unicorn horns. I believe their use
for removing bad statuses is fine, since there's few alternatives
(mostly minor); the problem is that their use for recovering stats
entirely eclipses other objects. My suggestion would be to implement
the same kind of thing that exists for recovering level loss by
blessed full healing: only allow unicorn horns to recover a maximum of
half the points lost from any stat, with any further points requiring
restore ability (spell or potion).

If this sounds too complicated (and it'd require more bookkeeping, I
agree), another option would be to give unicorn horns a timeout,
similar to artifact invocation, making their automatic use less
casual. Having it individual to the horn would just lead to people
swapping between several, so you'd need to make it a global timeout
for all horns.

